🎬 I Tested Every MiniMax H3 Speed Up So You Don't Have To

Four attention modes and thirteen turbo LoRAs for MiniMax H3, all run on the same RTX 5090 with the same seed, same prompt, same 1344x768 five second clip. Every result lands on a live leaderboard, speed and quality scored separately, for both FL2VA (first/last frame to video) and Ref2VA (reference to video).

Before the numbers I break down what the words actually mean: what attention is and why SDPA, Comfy Kitchen, SageAttention and SLA differ, what a turbo LoRA does to the model, what steps and shift are, and why speed and quality are a tradeoff instead of a free upgrade. Then we find out which lever actually moves your render time, and it's probably not the one you think.

